estament","chapters":1,"verseCount":13,"slug":"2-john"},{"book":"3 John","testament":"New Testament","chapters":1,"verseCount":14,"slug":"3-john"},{"book":"Jude","testament":"New Testament","chapters":1,"verseCount":25,"slug":"jude"},{"book":"Revelation","testament":"New Testament","chapters":22,"verseCount":404,"slug":"revelation"}],"jesusHub":"# Jesus Christ \"And beginning at Moses and all the prophets, he expounded unto them in all the scriptures the things concerning himself.\" — Luke 24:27 (KJV) \"Search the scriptures; for in them ye think ye have eternal life: and they are they which testify of me.\" — John 5:39 (KJV) Every book in this vault links here — because every book in the Bible points here. Open the graph view and you'll see it: sixty-six books, one Person at the center. ## The Cross and the Empty Tomb The Bible is not a collection of moral tales. It is one story with one hero and one hinge: \"For I delivered unto you first of all that which I also received, how that Christ died for our sins according to the scriptures; And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures.\" — 1 Corinthians 15:3–4 (KJV) Christ died for our sins — the Cross is where the guilt of every altar, every lamb, every broken law from Genesis to Malachi was laid on the sinless Substitute. He rose again the third day — the Resurrection is God's public receipt that the payment was accepted. He is alive. ## The Gift If you're reading this and you've never received Him — this whole vault was built for you: \"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.\" — John 3:16 (KJV) Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ — that He died for your sins and rose again — and call on His name: \"For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved.\" — Romans 10:13 (KJV) That's it. Not works, not religion, not cleaning yourself up first. Faith in the crucified, risen Son. Tell Him now, in your own words. ## The Two Testaments - Old Testament — the promise: Christ concealed, anticipated, prefigured - New Testament — the fulfillment: Christ revealed, crucified, risen, returning"}